  "body": "**What happens:** `crates/app/tests/index_swing.rs` (and the new `index_swing_horizontal.rs` in PR #1020) declare `Gate map (M4.4): covers app::posting (index_swing, verification_gate), ...`. The swing law is the top-level module `app::posting_index_swing` (`crates/app/src/posting_index_swing.rs`), not a submodule of `app::posting`. So `cargo xtask gate quick` does not select `index_swing` for a change to the swing law; the #818 worker had to run it by hand. The same `app::posting (<file stem>)` spelling may hide other `posting_*.rs` siblings (`posting_mounts`, ...).\n\n**Why P1:** the index swing is a post-gate safety law (it refuses a G0 index that would swing the work into the tool). A change to it can pass the quick gate without its pinning suite running, which is the class of gap #922 closed for moved modules.\n\n**Done means:** every suite whose map names `app::posting (<x>)` for a module that is really `app::posting_<x>` names the real module; an xtask unit test pins that a change to `crates/app/src/posting_index_swing.rs` selects `index_swing` (and the #1020 suite once it lands). Check against PR #965's header rewrite to avoid conflicts.\n",
